implement a RUF compilation failure recovery tool that can recover up to 90% of the failure. We believe our techniques, findings, and tools can help to stabilize the Rust compiler, ultimately enhancing the security and reliability of the Rust ecosystem.\n\nIn this repository, we describe how we use our tools to collect, generate, and analyze data to support our RUF research. We also provide complete data behind the paper, give guidance to reproduce the data, and validate our tools. The data we used are from another repository.", "is_draft": false, "publication_date_l10n_long": "January 2024", "publication_date_l10n_medium": "Jan 2024", "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.8289279", "relation_type": {"id": "requires", "title_l10n": "Requires"}, "resource_type": {"id": "dataset", "title_l10n": "Dataset"}, "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "https://sites.google.com/view/ruf-study/home", "relation_type": {"id": "isdescribedby", "title_l10n": "Is described by"}, "resource_type": {"id": "other", "title_l10n": "Other"}, "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://github.com/ZJU-SEC/Cargo-Ecosystem-Monitor", "relation_type": {"id": "ispartof", "title_l10n": "Is part of"}, "resource_type": {"id": "software", "title_l10n": "Software"}, "scheme": "url"}], "resource_type": {"id": "software", "title_l10n": "Software"}, "rights": [{"description_l10n": "The Creative Commons Attribution license allows re-distribution and re-use of a licensed work on the condition that the creator is appropriately credited.", "icon": "cc-by-icon", "id": "cc-by-4.0", "props": {"scheme": "spdx", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode"}, "title_l10n": "Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International"}], "updated_date_l10n_long": "June 23, 2024", "version": "v0.0.2"}, "updated": "2024-06-23T05:22:29.308686+00:00", "versions": {"index": 2, "is_latest": true}}' data-preview='false'>
